{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/366894-are-there-any-stories-about-making-pacts","id":366894,"title":"Are there any stories about making Pacts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-11T20:32:35-08:00","id":366894,"title":"Are there any stories about making Pacts?","content":"Are there any stories that include Demons persuading people to sign pacts? I tried to do this in my chronicle, and I realized that I have no idea how a Demon would approach someone, explain the pact, and make the sale, all without being compromised.<br /> <br /> One story in Demon Interface glazed over it, and the guy was on his deathbed, another had Pacts made, but it was to people who already had seen their friend, a demon, burned...<br /> <br /> It seems like it would be hard to explain to someone what exactly they are signing and dealing with &quot;deals with a devil&quot; criticisms, etc.<br /> <br /> (if it does not exist maybe it could make it into the Storytellers guide)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T21:19:19-08:00","id":366937,"title":"","content":"Watch The Booth at the End on Hulu.<br /> <br /> Read a book on negotiation, body language, social engineering etc.<br /> <br /> Go to a used car lot, watch the salesman approach another customer, listen to his or her pitch, etc.<br /> <br /> Flowers of Hell, pg 91 has two demon discussing a soul pact, as well as some trade-craft for isolating and preparing the target.<br /> <br /> Think of it like an asset recruitment for any intelligence agency: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Spot someone who has something you want.</li> <li>Find out what they want (the entire human race wants something)</li> <li>Research them, find out what kind of person they are, try to deduce how they will react.</li> <li>Approach them. Interact with them, sound them out.</li> <li>Pitch the deal. This is the moment of vulnerability, but you can give misleading information about who you are (&quot;Hi, I'm an attorney, let's discuss getting rid of those drug charges&quot; etc.).</li> <li>Close the deal.</li> <li>Get away without leaving trails.</li> </ol><br /> There are dozens of embeds that make the process easier, more reliable, and safer for the demon involved: Heart's Desire, Loose Lips, etc.<br /> <br /> For compromises: Compartmentalization is key. Remember, you get compromise if someone sees you acting out of character, which is harder to gauge if they don't know your cover. &quot;Mysterious stranger at the bar&quot; has wider latitude for unusual behavior than &quot;Jacob Kowalski, English teacher at Sightner High School, Boy Scout scout master, and sexy, sexy single bachelor&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 01-13-2015, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T21:47:34-08:00","id":366969,"title":"","content":"I think part of my problem is between 5 and 6, how do you explain that it's for &quot;part of your life&quot; or something, or maybe Demons mostly don't explain that at all... but then how do they explain what exactly it is that they're going to do...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T22:18:12-08:00","id":367020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/366894-are-there-any-stories-about-making-pacts?p=366969#post366969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of my problem is between 5 and 6, how do you explain that it's for &quot;part of your life&quot; or something, or maybe Demons mostly don't explain that at all... but then how do they explain what exactly it is that they're going to do...</div> </div> </div> </div>Just don't let on like it's a &quot;part of your life&quot; and &quot;for my cover&quot; and such. Use misleading language (demon's are, after all, masters of language) and misdirection.<br /> <br /> Instead of &quot;Hey, I want to take over your job and add that aspect to my cover, in exchange I'll give you x amount of money (equal to 2 dots increased resources)&quot;<br /> say: &quot;Hey, looks like you're stuck in a dead-end job and unhappy. I'll give you x amount of money (2 dots), and all it will cost you is a job you don't like anyway.&quot;<br /> <br /> Instead of &quot;I'll get you allies in the courts so your criminal record goes away, in exchange I want Amanda, your girlfriend of two years.&quot;<br /> say: &quot;It's tough to get a job with all those background checks, isn't it? How bout we make those disappear, all it'll cost you is Amanda.&quot;<br /> <br /> Instead of &quot;I can make you magically beautiful so you can have any job you want, all I want is the relationship you have with your mother.&quot;<br /> say: &quot;Showbiz is rough without the looks, huh? I know a great doctor, he doesn't take money. All he'd ask is that you never see your estranged mother again.&quot; (this one might be a bit more elaborate, with a fake &quot;surgery&quot; to be convincing)<br /> <br /> Those are really quick examples, so they might be slightly off but the point is don't bother saying anything supernatural at all, because they don't have to know that part. They can think you're just some guy that arranges things.<br /> <br /> Finally, when they're reading the contract they have to sign, rush them. &quot;You <i>could</i> sit here and read through all that, but I really have places to be, so why don't we make this fast.&quot; Get up to leave, take a step away. Thing about wants and desires is that humans tend to not think really hard when you hand them something they truly want, then threaten to take it away. Being confronted by your greatest wishes is something that makes anyone hard-pressed to look too deeply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T20:35:22-08:00","id":368215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/366894-are-there-any-stories-about-making-pacts?p=366969#post366969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of my problem is between 5 and 6, how do you explain that it's for &quot;part of your life&quot; or something, or maybe Demons mostly don't explain that at all... but then how do they explain what exactly it is that they're going to do...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>DtD pg. 190</b><br /> <i>A contract must always be signed willingly by a human\u2019s own hand, but this does not preclude coercion. Any form of influence or direct intimidation (i.e., \u201cSign this or I will kill you\u201d) is allowed, as long as the mortal signs the contract herself. Using mind-control powers to force an assignee\u2019s hand voids any deal made. The mortal doesn\u2019t need to know what exactly it is she is signing. If she fails to read the fine print, it\u2019s on her head. Clever demons use this to their advantage, although as much as they lie, the person in question still must know the terms of the deal. Misdirection and manipulation are both common tactics in making pacts.</i><br /> <br /> There are multiple ways to go about actually asking for part of their life. Because it has to be on paper, you could hide it in legalize. I personally prefer more a direct approach. Find some one in a vulnerable moment, and offer them something to good to be true. You don't even have to go detail. Nothing in the rules requires you to tell them what you are, or what will happen to the part of their life that you take. You might have to give some reassurances that nothing bad will happen to the person or thing that they lose. You don't even have to tell them you're keeping it, just that they need to give it up to make the deal happen.<br /> <br /> Or you might try to get them when they're just a bit out of it, like the drunk at the bar. Think the Urban Legend with the guy that wakes up in the Hotel room missing a kidney, but instead of an organ, it's his girlfriend that can't remember him.<br /> <br /> THe important thing is to remember that your storyteller is willing to work with you to make it happen, so don't worry about your character as coming off as too crazy. If you get to that point, they're likely to roll with it.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for inspiration<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deals_with_the_Devil_in_popular_culture\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/38/Twardowski_z_diablem.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deals_with_the_Devil_in_popular_culture\" target=\"_blank\"> Deals with the Devil in popular culture - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deals_with_the_Devil_in_popular_culture\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deals_with_the_Devil_in_popular_culture </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DealWithTheDevil\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...alWithTheDevil</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1279-badger-king","name":"Badger King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1279_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T01:17:21-08:00","id":368412,"title":"","content":"One of my players developed this scheme: Ms. Spider created a student as her cover at the local university whom would be a psychology major. This cover was made primarily for acquiring pacts with ease through the scheme. She'd approach another student and claim that her pre-printed contracts were thought-experiments or surveys into the student psychology on campus and that these were all part of her project or thesis or class. If she spotted a mark that had more to give or whom she believed she could get more out of she'd approach personally and pretend to counsel them.<br /> <br /> An idea I had for another demon, whom sadly I have yet to use in a game, was one whom played the head of an abstinence circle at a local church. She'd acquire her members guilty habits for various, more seedy covers by &quot;taking&quot; what they wanted to abstain from and &quot;giving&quot; what they hoped God might give. &quot;I will give up my porn addiction in the hope that God might make me more attractive to a wholesome woman.&quot; resulting in stealing an addiction to apply to a cover by giving a 2 dot bonus to Socialise. Internally, she'd justify it with 'Well, God really is giving them what they want. It just takes a little nudging from me to get Him going on the matter.'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}